# xlade cat

Run `xlade cat --help` for the live command help.

---

## Basic viewing

```bash
xlade cat path/to/File.lean
xlade cat first.lean second.lean
xlade cat path/to/File.lean --head 20
xlade cat path/to/File.lean --tail 20
xlade cat path/to/File.lean --lines 10-25
xlade cat path/to/File.lean --pager
```

---

## Flags:

```bash
-n, --number                                                                    # Number every output line
-b, --number-nonblank                                                           # Number non-blank lines
-s, --squeeze-blank                                                             # Suppress repeated blank lines
-E, --show-ends                                                                 # Show `$` at line ends
-T, --show-tabs                                                                 # Show tabs as `^I`
-v, --show-nonprinting                                                          # Show non-printing characters
-A, --show-all                                                                  # Equivalent to -vET
```

---

## Lean Inspection:

```bash
xlade cat File.lean --summary                                                   # Reports the path, line count, imports, declarations, sorry count, and Lean check status
xlade cat File.lean --imports                                                   # Lists imported modules with line numbers
xlade cat File.lean --symbols                                                   # Lists common declarations such as theorems, definitions, structures, namespaces, and examples
xlade cat File.lean --context 42 --context-lines 5                              # Marks the requested source line and displays nearby lines
xlade cat File.lean --diagnostics                                               # Runs lean on the file
xlade cat File.lean --diagnostics --explain                                     # Uses the database in `tools/errors/` to add human explanations to diagnostics
```
---

## Advanced Usage:

```bash
xlade cat --experiment exp-000                                                  # List Lean files in an experiment
xlade cat --experiment exp-000 File.lean --summary                              # Inspect a path relative to an experiment directory and summarise
xlade cat --experiment exp-000 --all --summary                                  # Inspect every Lean file discovered in an experiment with a selected report
```

